      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LAKEVIEW IAN (8) drew a squeeze box and was game in defeat when a close second, 1.5 lengths from the winner Paw Maud (33.07) at Traralgon. Recorded one of the quickest times on the card last start despite being beaten. Can find winning form. DERRY (7) has been settling off the speed lately, finishing fifth (42.45) last time in a Grade 5 at Sandown. Solid record at the distance winning two races. Likely to play a prominent role. ENGELKE ROAD (1) settled back off the inside but went through his gears strongly to find the frame with a 1.5 lengths third (33.37) at Traralgon in Grade 4/5. Recorded one of the quickest times on the card last start despite being beaten. Hard to beat again. YOUNG RUFUS (5) is a last start winner and can go on with it.",
